*.fasl

# Runtime state, not source: the gateway rewrites this as terminals enrol and lapse, and it holds
# device pubkeys.  Tracking it made every session show up as a diff.
demo/glass-webrtc/.glass-devices

# Holds live TURN credentials and the box's allowlist.  The launcher is deliberately NOT in the
# repo; see DEPLOY.md / README for the variables it sets.
demo/glass-webrtc/gw-keepalive.sh

# site-url.env is GONE, not merely ignored.  It was publish.lisp's way of telling the gateway which
# path had just been published, and it stopped having a reader the day the `link' command moved
# into the desktop -- which nothing could detect, because a file cannot report that nobody is
# reading it.  Publishing happens in the image that mints now (glass :glass/site), so the tag is a
# variable; what survives is a one-line memo at ~/.glass/site-url that the same image reads at its
# next cold start, outside any checkout.  The ignore line is kept for one release so an old working
# copy does not suddenly show it as untracked.
demo/glass-webrtc/site-url.env

# Build output + node_modules if someone points NSITE_BUILD inside the checkout.
demo/glass-webrtc/nsite-build/
demo/glass-webrtc/node_modules/
